WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.617
A frame describes which rows within an ordered partition contribute to the current calculation.

00:00:07.617 --> 00:00:14.017
For a running total, the frame may start at the beginning and end at the current row.

00:00:14.017 --> 00:00:20.132
For a three-row moving average, it may include two preceding rows and the current row.

00:00:20.132 --> 00:00:26.662
For some value functions, the frame may need to extend to the end of the partition.

00:00:26.662 --> 00:00:31.422
Window functions preserve detail rows while calculating across a related set.

00:00:31.422 --> 00:00:35.907
PARTITION BY defines independent groups, ORDER BY defines sequence,

00:00:35.907 --> 00:00:39.747
and the frame defines which neighboring rows participate.

00:00:39.747 --> 00:00:44.546
Those three choices are part of the business rule, not just syntax.
